						<div class="card-header d-flex px-4 py-2 align-items-center justify-content-between btnv btn-link" id="heading_collapseTTS_5" data-toggle="collapse" data-target="#collapseTTS_5" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseTTS_5">
							<div class="heading d-flex align-items-center">
								<h3>Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) support?</h3>
							</div>
							<div class="icon d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center">
								<i class="fa" aria-hidden="true"></i>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div id="collapseTTS_5" class="collapse show" aria-labelledby="heading_collapseTTS_5">
							<div class="card-body p-4 pt-md-3">
								<p>
								Full SSML support. You can send Speech Synthesis Markup Language (SSML) in your Text-to-Speech request to allow for more customization in your audio response by providing details on pauses, and audio formatting for acronyms, dates, times, abbreviations, addresses, or text that should be censored. See the Speech-to-Text <a href="https://cloud.google.com/text-to-speech/docs/ssml" target="_blank" title="Google's SSML tutorial">SSML tutorial</a> for more information and code samples.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
